kosha raga-varga

  -- cluster for raga concepts: raga, arohana, avarohana, vadi-swara, nyasa, gamaka.
  -- a raga is a melodic framework — a specific selection and ordering of swaras.
  -- arohana (ascent) and avarohana (descent) define the raga's movement through swara space.

  "sangeetham-varga-vishesa"
  "subanta-swarupa"

  -- sangati roots
  "krama-swarupa"   -- raga IS krama: arohana and avarohana are ordered sequences of swaras
  "viveka-yukta"    -- ragas are distinguished from each other by viveka of swara choice and gamakas
  "avastha-yukta"   -- vadi (dominant), samvadi (consonant), vivadi (dissonant) are relational states
  "gati-yukta"      -- melodic movement (arohana/avarohana) is gati through swara space
  "naada-yukta"     -- ragas are expressions of naada: organised primordial sound

done
